    "id": "rk_a1639d6a2ea5ace04fff",
    "text": "*Isaiah 7:14 — almah. \"Virgin\" (ESV, NIV, KJV) vs. \"young woman\" (NRSV, RSV, JPS). The Hebrew almah means a young woman of marriageable age; Hebrew has a specific word for virgin, betulah, and it is not used here. The Septuagint rendered it parthenos*, which does carry \"virgin,\" and Matthew quotes the Greek. When the RSV printed \"young woman\" in 1952, copies were publicly burned. The scholarly reading is not controversial; the theological stakes are.",
    "raw_text": "**Isaiah 7:14 — *almah*.** \"Virgin\" (ESV, NIV, KJV) vs. \"young woman\" (NRSV, RSV, JPS). The Hebrew *almah* means a young woman of marriageable age; Hebrew has a specific word for virgin, *betulah*, and it is not used here. The Septuagint rendered it *parthenos*, which does carry \"virgin,\" and Matthew quotes the Greek. When the RSV printed \"young woman\" in 1952, copies were publicly burned. **The scholarly reading is not controversial; the theological stakes are.**",
    "provenance_type": "CLAUDE",
